          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            Model completeness is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/property"} property
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/first-order+theories"} first-order theories
            (in the same way that
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/existential+closedness"} existential closedness
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/property"} property
            of
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/first-order+structures"} first-order structures
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ACF"} ACF
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraically+closed+fields"} algebraically closed fields
          %p
            As discussed in Hodges’
            = succeed ":" do
              %a{:href => "#Hodges1993"} Model theory
          %blockquote
            %p
              In the early 1950s
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Abraham+Robinson"} Abraham Robinson
              noticed that certain maps studied by algebraists are in fact
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elementary+embeddings"} elementary embeddings
            %p
              In the course of this quest he introduced the notions of model complete theories, companionable theories and
              = succeed "." do
                %span.newWikiWord
                  model companions
                  %a{:href => "/nlab/new/model+companion"} ?
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            We say a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/first-order+theory"} first-order theory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            is
            %em model complete
            if every embedding (not necessarily elementary) between models of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            %em is
            elementary.
          %p
            The following characterization appears as Theorem 8.3.1 in (
            %a{:href => "#Hodges1993"}> Hodges93
            ):
          .num_theorem
            %h6#theorem Theorem
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              be as above. The following are equivalent:
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi T
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
                  is model complete.
              %li
                %p
                  Every model of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi T
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
                  is
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/existentially+closed+model"} existentially closed
              %li
                %p
                  For every embedding
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                        %mo ↪
                        %mi B
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \hookrightarrow B
                  where
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                  and
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi B
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
                  model
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi T
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elementary+extension"} elementary extension
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi D
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
                  of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                  and an embedding
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi g
                        %mo :
                        %mi B
                        %mo →
                        %mi D
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g : B \to D
                  such that the triangle commutes.
              %li
                %p
                  Every
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/existentially+closed+model"} existential formula
                  is equivalent (mod
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi T
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/existentially+closed+model"} universal formula
              %li
                %p
                  Every formula is equivalent (mod
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi T
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
          %h2#examples Examples
          %ul
            %li
              Since
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantifier+elimination"} quantifier elimination
              is equivalent to
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/substructure+completeness"} substructure completeness
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ACF"} ACF
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/DLO"} DLO
              = succeed "," do
                %span.newWikiWord
                  RCF
                  %a{:href => "/nlab/new/RCF"} ?
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/countable+random+graph"} countable random graph
              are all model complete (and so their models are
              = succeed ".)" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/existentially+closed"} existentially closed
          %h2#remarks Remarks
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                A theory
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
                is model complete if and only if for every
                %em model
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                of
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi T
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantifier-free+diagram"} quantifier-free diagram
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi T
                        %mrow
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "sans-serif"}
                            %mi Diag
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi A
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_{\mathsf{Diag}(A)}
                (whose models are precisely the models of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
                containing
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                as an embedded substructure) is
                = succeed "." do
                  %em complete
            %li
              %p
                Analogously, a theory
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
                is
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/substructure+complete"} substructure complete
                if and only if for every model
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
                and every
                %em substructure
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi B
                        %mo ⊆
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B \subseteq A
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantifier-free+diagram"} quantifier-free diagram
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi T
                        %mrow
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "sans-serif"}
                            %mi Diag
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi B
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_{\mathsf{Diag}(B)}
                is
                = succeed "." do
                  %em complete
            %li
              %p
                A model complete theory is an “existentially closed theory” in the sense that all of its models are
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/existentially+closed+model"} existentially closed models
            %li
              %p
                As mentioned above,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/substructure+completeness"} substructure completeness
                implies model completeness because every elementary submodel is also a substructure. The proposition below shows that the converse holds with some additional assumptions.
          %h2#model_completeness__amalgamation_property_implies_substructure_completeness Model completeness + amalgamation property implies substructure completeness
          #substructureconverse.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              Suppose the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/first-order+theory"} first-order theory
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              in the language
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℒ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{L}
              is model complete and has the property that for any two models
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ⊧
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X,Y \models T
              and a mutual
              = succeed "-substructure" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℒ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{L}
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo ↪
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \hookrightarrow X,Y
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/span"} span
              in the category of
              = succeed "-structures" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℒ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{L}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocone"} cocone
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Z
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Z
              which is also a model of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            %p
              Then
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              is
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/substructure+complete"} substructure complete
          %p
            This property of being able to “amalgamate” the models
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            over the common substructure
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is sometimes called the
            = succeed "," do
              %strong amalgamation property
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fraisse+limit"} Fraisse limit
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              be a substructure of some model
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi M
                      %mo ⊧
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M \models T
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantifier-free+diagram"} quantifier-free diagram
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              to form
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi T
                        %mrow
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "sans-serif"}
                            %mi Diag
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi A
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_{\mathsf{Diag}(A)}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi φ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \varphi
              is a sentence which is undecided by
              = succeed ";" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi T
                        %mrow
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "sans-serif"}
                            %mi Diag
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi A
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_{\mathsf{Diag}(A)}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
              be models of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi T
                      %mrow
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "sans-serif"}
                          %mi Diag
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_{\mathsf{Diag}(A)}
              which witness this, so that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ⊧
                    %mi φ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \models \varphi
              while
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Y
                      %mo ⊧
                      %mo ¬
                      %mi φ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y \models \neg \varphi
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Z
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Z
              amalgamate
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
              over
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %p
              By
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+completeness"} model completeness
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi T
                      %mrow
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "sans-serif"}
                          %mi Diag
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_{\mathsf{Diag}(X)}
              of
              = succeed "-models" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elementary+embedding"} elementarily
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is complete. Abuse notation and replace the instances of constants from
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi φ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \varphi
              with their images in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi T
                      %mrow
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "sans-serif"}
                          %mi Diag
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊧
                    %mi φ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_{\mathsf{Diag}(X)} \models \varphi
              or
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi T
                        %mrow
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "sans-serif"}
                            %mi Diag
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi X
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ⊧
                      %mo ¬
                      %mi φ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_{\mathsf{Diag}(X)} \models \neg \varphi
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              certainly embeds itself and
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo ⊧
                      %mi φ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \models \varphi
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi T
                        %mrow
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "sans-serif"}
                            %mi Diag
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi X
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ⊧
                      %mi φ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_{\mathsf{Diag}(X)} \models \varphi
            %p
              Similarly,
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi T
                      %mrow
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "sans-serif"}
                          %mi Diag
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi Y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊧
                    %mo ¬
                    %mi φ
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_{\mathsf{Diag}(Y)} \models \neg \varphi.
            %p
              Now, on one hand, the theory
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi T
                      %mrow
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "sans-serif"}
                          %mi Diag
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∪
                    %msub
                      %mi T
                      %mrow
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "sans-serif"}
                          %mi Diag
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi Y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_{\mathsf{Diag}(X)} \cup T_{\mathsf{Diag}(Y)}/A
              (where we glue along the copies of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "sans-serif"}
                      %mi Diag
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathsf{Diag}(X)
              and
              = succeed ")" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "sans-serif"}
                        %mi Diag
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathsf{Diag}(Y)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi φ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \varphi
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo ¬
                      %mi φ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \neg \varphi
            %p
              On the other hand, this theory axiomatizes the class of amalgams of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
              over
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              in the category of
              = succeed "-structures" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℒ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{L}
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Z
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Z
